&lt;p&gt;Please be aware that Zynga does not conduct job interviews or make job offers over third-party messaging apps such as Telegram, WhatsApp, or others.&amp;nbsp; Zynga also does not engage in any financial exchanges during the recruitment or onboarding process, and will never ask a candidate for their personal or financial information over an app or other unofficial chat channel.&amp;nbsp; Any attempt to do so may be the result of a scamp or phishing attack, and you should not engage.&amp;nbsp; Zynga’s&amp;nbsp; in-house recruitment team will only contact individuals through their official Company email addresses (i.e., via a zynga.com, take2games.com, naturalmotion.com, smallgiantgames.com, themavens.com, gram.gs email domain).&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is building economic infrastructure for the internet. We help organizations of every size move money, manage revenue, and build global financial services.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Public Sector team builds Stripe’s presence in markets where organizations deliver essential services to millions of people. In the UK, public sector organizations collect taxes and tuition, enable transit, distribute funds, support charitable giving, and modernize citizen services. The team helps these organizations improve how they collect, manage, and disburse funds.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the UK Public Sector Lead, you will build and lead Stripe’s public sector go-to-market motion in the UK. You will define how Stripe serves central government, local government, devolved administrations, public bodies, higher education, utilities, transport, charities and not-for-profit organizations, and adjacent regulated organizations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will combine market knowledge, commercial judgment, and operational leadership to build trusted relationships, win meaningful business, and establish the operating model needed to serve public sector customers. This role reports to the Global Head of Public Sector and will help launch Stripe’s UK public sector motion in 2027.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define Stripe’s UK public sector strategy, including priority segments, customer problems,&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; routes to market, commercial opportunities, and the capabilities needed to succeed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build relationships across government, public bodies, procurement ecosystems, industry associations, systems integrators, and advisory partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with senior customer decision-makers to understand their payment, revenue, digital service, and financial infrastructure needs, and develop solutions with Stripe teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Guide strategic opportunities through public sector procurement, contracting, security, compliance, and stakeholder alignment requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Legal, Compliance, Risk, Go-to-Market, Alliances and Channels, Product, Engineering, Finance, and Operations to prepare Stripe to support public sector customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Turn recurring market requirements into priorities for onboarding, risk, contracting, procurement, implementation, support, and product development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build the positioning, account strategy, partner ecosystem, sales plays, internal processes, and success metrics that support growth in the UK and inform Stripe’s global public sector strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in or selling to the UK public sector, including government, public bodies, education, transport, utilities, charities and not-for-profit organizations, or other regulated institutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Established senior relationships across the UK public sector, its partner ecosystem, and relevant procurement or policy communities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience delivering complex outcomes across multiple stakeholders and working through public sector procurement, contracting, compliance, risk, and implementation requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading senior cross-functional stakeholders across Legal, Compliance, Risk, Product, Sales, Partnerships, and Operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills, strategic judgment, and experience working directly on market-building initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience launching a product, organization, market, vertical, or strategic go-to-market motion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in payments, financial services, enterprise software, digital transformation, or platform technology&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with UK public procurement frameworks and common contracting vehicles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with systems integrators, consulting firms, implementation partners, or public sector technology ecosystems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience turning customer and regulatory requirements into scalable products, processes, or commercial models&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;About Eucalyptus&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re on a mission to make good health last a lifetime. More than 1 billion people live with obesity worldwide, driving preventable chronic conditions. We&#39;re here to build better long-term care.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Eucalyptus is now part of Hims &amp;amp; Hers, the global leader in personalised health and wellness.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Euc is the company behind Juniper, one of the world&#39;s largest weight-management programs combining GLP-1 medication with personalised nutrition, movement support, and clinician-led care from prescribers, nurses, health coaches, pharmacists, and dietitians. Our published clinical research shows that our combined clinical and behavioural approach helps patients lose significantly more weight during their treatment with Juniper by four times.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Our Growth Story:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Supporting patients living with obesity across our 5 markets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Received selective NICE endorsement to provide services to the NHS&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tailored our offering to thousands of patients in Australia, the UK, Germany, Japan and Canada.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;About Eucalyptus&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re on a mission to make good health last a lifetime. More than 1 billion people live with obesity worldwide, driving preventable chronic conditions. We&#39;re here to build better long-term care.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Eucalyptus is now part of Hims &amp;amp; Hers, the global leader in personalised health and wellness.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Euc is the company behind Juniper, one of the world&#39;s largest weight-management programs combining GLP-1 medication with personalised nutrition, movement support, and clinician-led care from prescribers, nurses, health coaches, pharmacists, and dietitians. Our published clinical research shows that our combined clinical and behavioural approach helps patients lose significantly more weight during their treatment with Juniper by four times.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Our Growth Story:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;130% YoY revenue growth and a 90% reduction in cash burn - culminating in our $1.15bn acquisition by Hims &amp;amp; Hers in 2026, giving us the platform to take long-term care global&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Supported over 350k patients living with obesity across our 5 markets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Received selective NICE endorsement to provide services to the NHS&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tailored our offering to thousands of patients in Australia, the UK, Germany, Japan and Canada.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We have strong foundations. But to reach more markets, more brands, and more patients, we need a growth platform that gives us capabilities we don&#39;t yet have.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This isn&#39;t about what to build on the surface. It&#39;s about what foundational capabilities unlock the next step change — in conversion, retention, and how fast a new market can go live. Sometimes that&#39;s personalisation. Sometimes authentication. Sometimes embedding AI into exactly the right moment in the patient journey. You&#39;ll figure that out, own the roadmap, and ship it. The roadmap doesn&#39;t exist yet — you&#39;ll define it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll work with a cross-functional squad of engineers and designers and:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and own the growth platform strategy and roadmap — the foundational capabilities that unlock conversion, activation, retention, and market scalability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate platform investments into business outcomes — every capability has a clear hypothesis for how it moves a growth metric, shipped incrementally and not after a six-month build&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Embed AI where it genuinely improves outcomes — identifying the moments where an intelligent layer makes the experience materially better&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enable dynamic experiences across landing pages, onboarding, and in-product surfaces — the CMS, feature flagging, and content infrastructure that lets teams move without engineering dependency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build a tech stack that launches a new market in weeks, not months&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a platform role, not an infrastructure role. You care about what the platform enables for patients and growth teams — and you ship incrementally to prove it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About you&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;re a product manager who&#39;s comfortable in the space between user experience and engineering infrastructure. You think in systems and capabilities — but you never lose sight of the patient on the other end, or the growth team trying to move a metric.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You don&#39;t treat platform work as a reason to slow down. You know how to slice a large capability into meaningful increments that ship value fast, and you hold yourself accountable to growth metrics even when the work lives under the surface.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid PM experience with meaningful time on platform, growth, data, or infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You hold the technical and commercial view at once — you know what&#39;s being built, why it matters to the patient, and how it moves a metric&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable with ambiguity — you can take &quot;we need to be better at personalisation&quot; and turn it into a sequenced, defensible roadmap without waiting to be told what to build&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Adaptable — requirements change and you move with them, without losing sight of where you&#39;re going&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable working with data teams — event tracking, user identity, and data models aren&#39;t foreign to you&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong cross-functional instincts — you build alignment across engineering, data, design, and growth without needing authority&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Genuinely curious about where AI actually belongs in a product experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Bonus points for healthcare experience, multi-market platform thinking, or building personalisation engines.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;So, why join Eucalyptus?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Make real impact, fast&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;- We build in the open together, which helps us learn and iterate more quickly to deliver high-quality outcomes faster than anyone else. Helping impact patients’ lives for the better from the moment you join Euc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location flexibility:&lt;/strong&gt; You can choose to work hybrid in Berlin or relocate to London, UK (we will pay for sponsorship!)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You’ll be supported to accelerate your career&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;- Regular feedback alongside our bi-annual performance reviews, a professional development budget &amp;amp; leave help ensure you have the support you need to level up. We’re committed to helping every Eucalypt reach their full potential.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You’ll work with others who are incredibly passionate about what they do&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;- Our talent bar is high, and our work ethic is strong. You’ll get to stretch yourself every day, be given autonomy to tackle interesting problems, and work amongst people who care deeply about our patients.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We also offer a range of benefits including&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;Your own stake in the business with our employee options program&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;Newly opened HQ in vibrant Old Street, designed for focus and collaboration or an office in Berlin!&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;A flexible hybrid setup: 3 days a week in office&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;A monthly wellness allowance, for you to spend on whatever wellness means to you&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;A yearly personal development budget and 3 extra days of leave to continuously up-skill yourself&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;25 days holiday + bank holidays with an enhanced parental leave policy&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;A fun office with regular socials including after-school sport, clubs, cycle kick-offs, and seasonal parties. We had our winter social in Paris last year! 🇫🇷&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;Your own MacBook and more!&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Want to hear more about what it’s like to work at Eucalyptus? Hear from our team&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://eucalyptus.vc/careers&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;or check us out on Instagram -----
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;At Eucalyptus, we value individuals from all backgrounds, experiences, and perspectives, and we embrace the unique qualities each person brings. When you apply, please let us know of any reasonable adjustments you may need during the interview process. We use AI-assisted tools across our business to help our teams work more efficiently, including within our recruitment process. These tools support our team — all hiring decisions are made by real people, and every application is reviewed by a member of our recruitment team.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;GitLab is the intelligent orchestration platform for DevSecOps. GitLab enables organizations to increase developer productivity, improve operational efficiency, reduce security and compliance risk, and accelerate digital transformation. More than 50 million registered users and more than 50% of the Fortune 100* trust GitLab to ship better, more secure software faster.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The same principles built into our products are reflected in how our team works: we embrace AI as a core productivity multiplier, with all team members expected to incorporate AI into their daily workflows to drive efficiency, innovation, and impact. GitLab is where careers accelerate, innovation flourishes, and every voice is valued. Our high-performance culture is driven by our values&amp;nbsp;and continuous knowledge exchange, enabling our team members to reach their full potential while collaborating with industry leaders to solve complex problems. &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OuZIb5zszQI&quot;&gt;Co-create the future with us&lt;/a&gt; as we build technology that transforms how the world develops software.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;*&lt;em&gt;Fortune 500® is a registered trademark of Fortune Media IP Limited, used under license. Claim based on GitLab data. Fortune 100 refers to the top 20% ranked companies in the 2025 Fortune 500 list, published in June 2025. Fortune and Fortune Media IP Limited are not affiliated with, and do not endorse products or services of GitLab.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;An overview of this role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Scale Ecosystem Sales Manager - AMER, you&#39;ll fuel GitLab&#39;s growth by turning our emerging partner ecosystem into a consistent, scalable source of new customers. You&#39;ll focus on partner-sourced Scale pipeline generation, designing and running repeatable partner-led campaigns, systematic account mapping, and whitespace analysis that surface new logo opportunities for GitLab. In this role, you&#39;ll work closely with Scale Account Executives, Field Marketing, regional sales leadership, and partners such as distributors, longtail resellers, and hyperscalers like AWS and Google Cloud to integrate partners throughout the sales cycle and accelerate marketplace transactions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll own programmatic partner engagement across your territory, from partner enablement and activation at scale to event-driven strategies and 1:many campaigns via partner portals and automated systems. Your work will directly support GitLab&#39;s Scale growth targets by building a measurable, partner-led demand engine. Along the way, you&#39;ll deepen your experience in partner ecosystem management, digital marketing-driven demand generation, and modern sales development methodologies, while contributing to business planning, pipeline forecasting, and clear reporting on partner impact.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive partner-sourced Scale pipeline generation through scalable partner programs, campaigns, and systematic account mapping initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Scale Account Executives, Field Marketing, and regional sales leaders to integrate partners into territory planning and demand generation activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Execute repeatable partner-led Scale campaigns aligned to regional territories, including industry plays, account blitzes, and market-specific roadshows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify whitespace and conduct detailed account mapping with partners to surface new logo opportunities and expand First Order reach.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain programmatic relationships with emerging partners, distributors, longtail partners, and hyperscaler partners such as Amazon Web Services (AWS) and Google Cloud, with a focus on new customer acquisition and marketplace transactions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support partner enablement and activation programs to scale contribution across multiple partners, including hyperscaler co-sell and marketplace acceleration initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Execute event-driven partner strategies, including partner alignment before events, lead capture during events, and pipeline conversion optimization after events.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage one-to-many partner engagement through partner portals and automated systems, providing weekly pipeline forecasts, partner-sourced opportunity reports, and clear insights into campaign performance and territory impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in sales development, business development, or partner-driven pipeline generation in a B2B environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Practical familiarity with partner ecosystems, including programmatic partner engagement and demand generation with distributors, longtail partners, and hyperscalers such as AWS and Google Cloud.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to design, execute, and optimize scalable, campaign-driven approaches to demand generation, including 1:many partner engagement and event-driven campaigns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using Salesforce and modern sales development or marketing automation tools to manage, forecast, and report on partner-sourced pipeline and campaign performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical skills to interpret campaign results, partner activation metrics, and territory impact, and translate insights into actionable plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Effective written and verbal communication skills, with a focus on clear, repeatable messaging and collaboration with account executives, field marketing, and regional sales leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interest in GitLab, open source software, and modern software development practices, with the ability to learn and use GitLab and related tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Openness to travel for partner events and field collaboration, and to apply transferable skills from related sales, partner, or digital marketing roles in a remote, results-focused environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Ecosystem Sales team focuses on building and scaling a high-impact partner network that drives Scale growth through partner-sourced pipeline and new logo acquisition. As a Scale - Ecosystem Sales Manager - AMER, you&#39;ll work as part of a distributed team that partners closely with Scale Account Executives, Field Marketing, regional sales leadership, and an emerging ecosystem of distributors, longtail partners, and hyperscalers. We collaborate asynchronously across regions to design and execute repeatable, campaign-driven motions, integrate partners into territory planning, and turn partner programs into measurable demand generation at scale. We are focused on expanding partner-sourced impact, improving systematic account mapping and whitespace identification, and building programmatic motions that make it easier for partners to acquire and grow new GitLab customers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#LI-JH1&lt;/p&gt;
